3. WHAT IS RELEASED, AND THE HONESTY CONTRACT
================================================================================

Released openly (CC BY-NC 4.0 for papers/docs/reviews, PolyForm
Noncommercial 1.0.0 for the scripts and bundled data):

    - papers/**            eight papers (XL, LIII-LIX)
    - docs/**              derivations, the claim-status ledger, the
                           verification manifest, the book-companion map
    - reviews/**           the unedited machine-referee reports
    - scripts/**           the verification suites and the only data file,
                           scripts/600cell_data.npz
    - run_all_verifications.sh
    - web/**               the single-file resonance explorer

These are sufficient for a serious reviewer to read every derivation, run
the full battery in about ten minutes, and re-derive every numerical claim
without trusting any cited paper.

The work is presented under a two-column honesty contract. The first
column is checkable: where a paper says "theorem", it means a statement
proved about the mathematical object — the 600-cell crystal — and confirmed
by the suites. The second column is the framework's bet: that this crystal
is the substrate of the physical world. That identification is argued, not
proved. The graded claim table (THEOREM / DERIVED / CONDITIONAL /
WITNESSED / TIE / OPEN, each with a falsifier) is docs/claim-status-ledger.md.

The framework is presented as a set of preprints and has NOT been
peer-reviewed.

